   "body": "### Description\n\nTrivy scans of container images are flagging a HIGH severity security vulnerability (`CVE-2026-56852`) in the `golang.org/x/text` dependency packaged inside the pre-compiled `gh` binary.\n\nThe vulnerability is an infinite loop in `golang.org/x/text/unicode/norm` (`norm.Iter`) when handling certain input, and was resolved in `golang.org/x/text` version `v0.39.0`. The current `gh` version `v2.96.0` was built against `golang.org/x/text` `v0.38.0` and bundles the vulnerable version.\n\n### Purpose\n\nCould you please trigger a dependency update to bump `golang.org/x/text` to `>= v0.39.0` and release a rebuild of the CLI so that downstream container builds scan cleanly without flagging this vulnerability?",
